  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Math\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Math\n       Program: commons-math\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/Math.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-math.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 106\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Math-69\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\nbb005b56ca0739c4c212804ba7a483c8164e78f1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2010-05-16 23:48:07 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nMATH-371\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MATH-371\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.math.stat.correlation.PearsonsCorrelationTest::testPValueNearZero\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError\n - org.apache.commons.math.stat.correlation.SpearmansRankCorrelationTest::testPValueNearZero\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.math.stat.correlation.PearsonsCorrelation\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: PearsonsCorrelation.getCorrelationPValues() precision limited by machine epsilon\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nSimilar to the issue described in MATH-201, using PearsonsCorrelation.getCorrelationPValues() with many treatments results in p-values that are continuous down to 2.2e-16 but that drop to 0 after that.\n\nIn MATH-201, the problem was described as such:\n> So in essence, the p-value returned by TTestImpl.tTest() is:\n> \n> 1.0 - (cumulativeProbability(t) - cumulativeProbabily(-t))\n> \n> For large-ish t-statistics, cumulativeProbabilty(-t) can get quite small, and cumulativeProbabilty(t) can get very close to 1.0. When \n> cumulativeProbability(-t) is less than the machine epsilon, we get p-values equal to zero because:\n> \n> 1.0 - 1.0 + 0.0 = 0.0\n\nThe solution in MATH-201 was to modify the p-value calculation to this:\n> p = 2.0 * cumulativeProbability(-t)\n\nHere, the problem is similar.  From PearsonsCorrelation.getCorrelationPValues():\n  p = 2 * (1 - tDistribution.cumulativeProbability(t));\n\nDirectly calculating the p-value using identical code as PearsonsCorrelation.getCorrelationPValues(), but with the following change seems to solve the problem:\n  p = 2 * (tDistribution.cumulativeProbability(-t));\n\nComments:\n\n[Phil Steitz]: Thanks for reporting this.\n\n[Phil Steitz]: Fixed in r944939.  Thanks!\n\n[Luc Maisonobe]: Closing issue as it was included in version 2.2, which has been released",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.math.stat.correlation.PearsonsCorrelation (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.math.stat.correlation.PearsonsCorrelation (fixed)\n@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@\n                 } else {\n                     double r = correlationMatrix.getEntry(i, j);\n                     double t = Math.abs(r * Math.sqrt((nObs - 2)/(1 - r * r)));\n-                    out[i][j] = 2 * (1 - tDistribution.cumulativeProbability(t));\n+                    out[i][j] = 2 * tDistribution.cumulativeProbability(-t);\n                 }\n             }\n         }"
}